 # CSG Operations on Implicit Functions
 
-Also called: CSG implicit surfaces, Constructive Solid Geometry, Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG) on Implicit Surfaces, Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG) with SDFs, Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG) with Signed Distance Bounds, Range Operations, SDF Boolean Operations, Set Operations, Union/Intersection via min/max
+Also called: CSG implicit surfaces, SDF Boolean Operations, Union/Intersection via min/max
 
 ## Overview
-Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG) on implicit functions composites multiple primitive shapes into a single implicit surface by applying Boolean logic to their distance fields [S1, unofficial, S5, unofficial]. This method allows the rendering of complex geometries composed of multiple primitives using a single field evaluation, which is essential for ray marching and bisection tracers [S1, unofficial]. Unlike explicit mesh operations, CSG on implicit functions reduces geometric composition to arithmetic operations on scalar values, enabling "free" normals and shadows derived from the resulting field's gradient [S4, unofficial]. It is distinguished from sibling primitives by its role as a compositing layer that combines the outputs of [Sphere Signed Distance Function](1237-sphere-signed-distance-function.md), [Signed Box Distance Function](1092-signed-box-distance-function.md), and other primitives into a unified scene representation [G].
