 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Smooth Union
-An alternative to the standard Union operation that creates a smooth transition (rounded fillets) between the edges of two shapes rather than a sharp crease [S3, S4, unofficial]. It takes an additional float parameter $k$ (typically 0 to 2) determining the degree of smoothness [S3, S4, unofficial]. It uses a polynomial function `smin(a, b, k)` instead of `min(a, b)` [S3, S4, unofficial].
