+### Constructive Solid Geometry (CSG) on Level Sets
+A voxel-based implementation of CSG operations that applies Boolean logic directly to discrete 3D grids [S6]. Union is implemented as `A_new(i,j,k) = min(A(i,j,k), B(i,j,k))`, intersection as `A_new(i,j,k) = max(A(i,j,k), B(i,j,k))`, and difference as `A_new(i,j,k) = max(A(i,j,k), -B(i,j,k))` [S6]. In user interface terms, intersection corresponds to a copy operation, union to a paste operation, and difference to a cut operation [S6].
